      frozen_profile: `contracts/vnext/subject-store-profile.v1.json` is 3,285 bytes with SHA-256 `606582eb83c6facb359385b00a4b13022a2a732489089fd049d74b37b43dca25`. The loader binds every policy literal, current contract-registry hash, campaign-projection profile hash, accepted schema and exact registry byte limit, layout, atomic-create rule, concurrency rule, rebuild rule, finite limit, and bounded result rule, then freezes the exported profile.
      accepted_boundary: Only artifact manifests, claims, outside-proof v2 records, P2P manifests, and release manifests are accepted. Every wire is independently accepted by both vNext validators, required canonical, and checked against its domain-separated subject and content identities. Private context is forbidden and receipts remain exclusively owned by the receipt DAG store. Unknown identity schemas and non-identity worker or companion messages fail closed.
      persistence_and_rebuild: Validated subject IDs select `subjects/sha256/{prefix}/{digest}.json`. Publication uses the shared no-follow, same-directory exclusive temporary, bounded write, file-fsync, hard-link create-if-absent, byte-identical reuse, directory-sync-or-explicit-Win32-unavailability, and exact-readback path. Rebuild caps active members at 2,048 and aggregate bytes at 64 MiB; quarantines malformed, unaccepted, identity-path-mismatched, unknown, and old interrupted entries; leaves fresh temporaries pending; and exposes no current or latest pointer. Active reads revalidate schema, subject ID, canonical hash, byte length, and exact bytes.
      artifact_identity_rule: Artifact manifests intentionally use the model artifact byte identity as subject ID while retaining a separate canonical-document hash. The store permits only one exact canonical manifest wire for an artifact ID. A different manifest with the same artifact ID is an immutable target conflict and can never replace the first bytes.
      verification: Focused subject-store tests passed 11/11; the receipt/content/artifact/inventory/threat neighborhood passed 59/59; the documentation-bound subset passed 17/17; and the final complete `npm run test:unit` gate passed 827/827 with zero failures and zero skips in 66.727 seconds. Independent-process publication, private/receipt rejection, conflict, interruption, quarantine, disk-full, post-startup tamper, restart withdrawal, and false-readback recovery are covered.
      source_hygiene: Profile SHA-256 and byte count, JavaScript syntax, staged diff, ASCII and NUL checks for all four new files, bounded secret/private-path scan for all eight changed files, source hashes, and zero changed production deployment-manifest members passed before commit. The 22,761-byte store source SHA-256 is `ead898073e02028208edf58326ba64805f748bc82ad0385e3d8f37eb6f2434ff`; the 13,778-byte test SHA-256 is `2a09984395ecb167d26c22d65a1c0286e09544fb20423da839bfd865556f5448`; and the 6,021-byte architecture page SHA-256 is `178ddefda295b04b675600ab325540c0a1cacaded3f91880723a08852e7afa63`.
