    phase_3_release_manifest_preparation_checkpoint:
      status: Commit `98d45bedfb24d6364e820a708030995ae6503a67` (`feat(evidence): prepare immutable release manifests`) is pushed and remote-exact. It extends the sole fresh-runner-bound surface with exact create-only `release_manifest.v2` preparation and explicitly returns `not-authorized`. It is not release authorization, deployment, public readback, publication, a live campaign receipt, or Phase 3 completion.
      release_truth_boundary: `prepareRelease` accepts one closed input and creates the same fresh sole-runner operation internally. It requires complete 20/50/25/40/20 projection truth; exact current snapshot membership; all 20 qualification-counted artifact hashes; exactly the qualified roots, one unqualified CycloneDX JSON 1.6 SBOM, and recursive dependency closure with no unrelated artifact; current-pass qualification, package, provenance, and claim evidence; package/provenance binding to the exact domain-separated artifact set and source revision; every current approved claim for the source revision; one current claim head per site/route/component/wording key; sorted bounded risks; and trusted-time-derived release date. No caller release ID, date, counter, verdict, authorization, deployment, readback, publication, or artifact-set digest is accepted.
      redaction_and_persistence: Every selected public subject/receipt, the strict canonical LF UTF-8 changelog, and the finalized release manifest are scanned against the protected equality list before unsafe bytes can be admitted. Public-safe scan receipts precede create-only manifest publication; a failure persists only bounded public-safe redaction evidence and never the unsafe manifest. Exact receipt/subject membership is revalidated before each final write, and create-only store reconstruction plus byte-exact readback is required before success.
