    phase_3_release_authorization_checkpoint:
      status: Code commit `ac0b9abc8137127775924732f64d1cd453ca4dbb` (`feat(evidence): verify release authorization`) is pushed and remote-exact. It extends the sole release surface with current vNext Ed25519 release-authorizer verification as a forward-only child of the prepared manifest. The documentation and redaction-only interruption regression in this containing checkpoint were verified after that code commit. This is not deployment, public readback, publication, live campaign evidence, or Phase 3 completion.
      authorization_truth_boundary: `authorizeRelease` accepts one closed data-only input: canonical authorization receipt bytes, canonical changelog bytes, exact prepared manifest ID, campaign/environment/source pins, trusted verification time, caller-pinned authority root and terminal, and the bounded protected equality list. It accepts no decision, verdict, status, deployment, publication, counter, stored projection, or mutable current pointer. It reconstructs the exact final attestation, runner start and terminal records, complete Rust-backed projection, original receipt and subject snapshots, selected release evidence, claims, and three preparation scans from create-only storage before authorization can be considered.
      authority_and_identity: The sole admitted authorization is one canonical `signature-envelope` receipt with role `release-authorizer`, domain `tinyrustlm.signature.release-authorizer.v1`, scope `release-authorization`, signed schema `tinyrustlm.vnext.release_manifest.v2`, exact manifest subject and release ID, exact canonical-content hash, matching campaign and source revision, and a finite current lifetime. The full vNext authority graph must verify under the caller-pinned root and terminal; signature validity, authority at issue, temporal currentness, current-evidence eligibility, empty stale reasons, and terminal-registry currentness are all mandatory. Retired, revoked, compromised, expired, duplicate, wrong-role, wrong-scope, wrong-release, drifted, or caller-decided evidence fails closed.
      redaction_persistence_and_restart: Preparation scans are replayed against the current protected list. Authorization bytes are scanned before persistence; unsafe bytes leave only one bounded public-safe failure scan. On success, the deterministic authorization-redaction receipt is create-only persisted before the signature receipt. Exact membership admits only prepared, prepared-plus-redaction, or prepared-plus-redaction-plus-signature states, proving restart recovery after the first write and byte-identical full replay. The immutable prepared manifest is never mutated. Success returns only `release-authorized-awaiting-deployment` and no `done`, deployed, published, or counter claim.
      frozen_facts: Release-surface profile is 6,613 bytes with SHA-256 `5dd859914628be87aaae2333d2d1c850b739d58fd0d16dec79f04b9fbb0cfa94`; release-surface source is 83,457 bytes with SHA-256 `ec0c03c9b767d2528fca96b4adc4f9386cccb67f60b8e4f10615da6678c3abe2`; the current 53,891-byte release-surface test is SHA-256 `418d87ca75b568ef2d812f5c9d023fce9c6eb5c65feb0ca48299f21b7d776322`; and the 9,950-byte authority fixture helper is SHA-256 `a74eb170d74559e7eaf714e095d57a0573662e230278bf3ee8a9a9586e86917c`. Runtime tests create ephemeral Ed25519 private keys only in process memory; no private key is committed.
      verification: The full release-surface suite passed 17/17 in 232.546 seconds, including restarted authorization, redaction-only interruption recovery, byte-identical replay, hostile caller fields, wrong bindings, expiry, retired authority, store drift, and unsafe authorization bytes. The adjacent authority/redaction/store/runner/currentness/registry/threat set passed 100/100. One first complete-unit run honestly failed a machine-checked documentation non-inflation sentence after the prose update; the exact invariant was restored, its focused test passed 3/3, and the corrected complete unit suite passed 856/856 with zero failures or skips in 265.541 seconds. The complete locked/offline Cargo workspace and doc tests passed; the focused `tinyrustlm-evidence` crate passed all 32 unit/integration tests; rustfmt and warnings-denied all-target workspace Clippy passed; and all six deterministic vNext generators replayed without worktree drift.
      documentation_and_deployment_truth: Contract guidance and the release-surface, signature-authority, inventory, threat-review, and Rust-currentness architecture pages now describe implemented authorization and preserve deployment/publication non-claims. Exactly zero of seven changed files intersected the 21 production source members in `tinyrustlm/deploy/web-deployment-manifest.v2.json`; the two generated release members also remain unchanged. Publishing unchanged bytes would fabricate a release, so no version, Updates entry, deployment, release receipt, public readback claim, or campaign counter was created.
      campaign_truth: Live progress remains 0/20 qualifying models, 0/50 deletion-backed clean-browser rounds, 0/25 authorized live memory rounds, 0/40 outside-network lane proofs, and 0/20 catalog announcements.
      exact_resume_boundary: Extend this same surface with strict forward-only deployment evidence and production HTTPS exact-byte/hash readback descendants. Then create only evidence-bound published claim.v2 descendants and site-publisher authorizations, cut every maintained entry point and current document to the completed replacement, and delete the superseded dashboard, final-attestation, release-authorization, release-evidence, public-readback, public-artifact-scope, and obsolete store paths without aliases or dual readers. In parallel, complete Rust/Win32 directory-flush evidence, compressed archive-member scanning, and protected equality-list custody.
    phase_3_exact_web_publication_graph_checkpoint:
      status: This containing source-controlled checkpoint cleanly supersedes the preproduction r4 `release_manifest.v2` family with one incompatible r5 `release_manifest.v3` family. It binds the exact static web publication graph before deployment without inventing a manifest self-hash or a generated pointer backreference. It is not deployment, public HTTPS readback, publication, live campaign evidence, or Phase 3 completion.
      exact_release_graph: Release v3 binds canonical public origin; one current-pass build receipt; exact changelog, deployment-manifest, security-header-profile, and publication-generator identities; every static public path, role, byte length, SHA-256, content type, cache policy, and security-header profile; exactly two generated publication-file descriptors; retired paths; total public bytes; offline capability; and the service-worker path. Static, generated, and retired paths are pairwise disjoint. Model-byte routes are forbidden. A cache policy of `immutable` is valid only when the public path contains the full content SHA-256; stable paths must revalidate or use no-store.
      acyclic_publication_model: The immutable manifest binds the inputs and deterministic descriptors for generated `.well-known/site-release.json` and `.well-known/site-release-history.json`, but not their final bytes because those documents must name the release identity. Release authorization signs the finalized manifest. Future deployment/readback and site-publisher descendants must bind the generated bytes forward from that authorization. No r4/v2 reader, alias, fallback, dual writer, migration, or self-referential compatibility object remains in active contracts, validators, Rust constants, vectors, or maintained architecture authority.
      frozen_contract_facts: Registry family `tinyrustlm-vnext-2026-08-09-r5` is 40,674 bytes with SHA-256 `dd1534f577f5468f94d4b3b4d7d8985751fd1ddc4a28a2ccee9f47462449bbf0`. Release descriptor SHA-256 is `0e03d1ab9445c9b668c92ade439aac71965267272bce854d88a10542a0deca58`; receipt descriptor SHA-256 is `55e8a406b618686d13452109331b627e084dedbbee464676ec0e4035d5319feb`; and release-surface profile is 7,637 bytes with SHA-256 `97cc27e2d54f8e1612702f2b55cdf7ab9d6e19d4a4ad280c6f73df81c77ec9d0`.
      transitive_identity_facts: Phase profile is 2,721 bytes with SHA-256 `924c515b2cddc081c9cbeac7e4c51fde213264ef2dff5bffcbc335430aafcbff`; projection profile is 4,857 bytes with SHA-256 `a5ed56eb0c0b924eaac3222bb814732bd36f2bfeae217477cf7549ae732d4ae9`; redaction profile is 3,473 bytes with SHA-256 `f1c5f00c631bb109f59c747abe0232468d783b3826acddc0019f91a1f746318a`; signature profile is 5,726 bytes with SHA-256 `c9f3c6813e3880ebff6c79d9975ba085405208260715b0c68eafdfb9cfcb5721`; subject-store profile is `8be12332d8c2936df74eed6548e03fff5d8f816479191814c639613444cc40c9`; artifact-store profile is `778743a9d36d3ca9be56c3037529a31766e76af56127b8cb02a36adb5ad61136`; generated WASM interface is `173fed5fadd66f5ca56f57e5a9718f27bf03d8671c3d98047b5c9ec473a2071d`; and runner profile is `d3eddd20b885556f6ad26804f122d60f7ff288c5bf4ef28a0929b52784f22323`.
      deterministic_corpus_and_vectors: The contract corpus is 195,068 bytes with SHA-256 `2c86c7da67d419b140f5de8b9d297707a6e47245a338db6dd9bcca55de912044`, containing 82 cases: 14 accepts, 68 rejects, and 164 matching dual-validator verdicts. Authority vectors are 434,761 bytes with SHA-256 `bf649b31e75c6ca6d4ec6587e760bbdd43b2e87bdcc7db7ed75fcc4ce787c757`; projection vectors are 1,494,464 bytes with SHA-256 `8a72ac1b2e4abd944e41c1c53a7d475e350d961e7b627127404b0508cf654734`; phase vectors are 74,756 bytes with SHA-256 `c583f55f0c81da4db08543b0a8e28ad4ee178a1a1a1169b6aeb3329bf67f7ee4`; signature vectors are 27,988 bytes with SHA-256 `22c0c0976209afdfc934939903d455a44d63312260881d0fe983cccadd20e413`; and offline vectors are 658,110 bytes with SHA-256 `29e72b60c92a2be4b340f71e90f5e1090d609dbf2702b633adb0738bcbe03007`.
      verification: Registry and conformance tests passed 13/13; the linked vector/parity set passed 16/16; the full release-surface suite passed 19/19; and the affected vNext neighborhood passed 161/161. Final complete `npm run test:unit` passed 858/858 with zero failures, skips, cancellations, or todos in 291.780 seconds. The complete locked/offline Rust workspace and all doc tests passed with zero failures, including 438 runtime tests and all cross-language evidence suites; focused 32-test evidence coverage, repository rustfmt, and warnings-denied all-target evidence Clippy also passed. Eight deterministic generators replayed successfully; 21 changed JSON files parsed; 22 changed JavaScript files passed syntax checks; `git diff --check` passed; active runtime/contract/architecture stale-r4/v2 search returned no matches; and zero of 23 production deployment-manifest members changed.
      documentation_and_deployment_truth: ADR-009 and every affected release, registry, inventory, threat, persistence, runner, redaction, authority, parity, offline-bundle, and subject-store architecture page were updated in the same change. The production web closure has no byte delta, so publishing unchanged bytes would fabricate a release. No site version, Updates entry, deployment, release receipt, public readback claim, or campaign counter was created.
      campaign_truth: Live progress remains 0/20 qualifying models, 0/50 deletion-backed clean-browser rounds, 0/25 authorized live memory rounds, 0/40 outside-network lane proofs, and 0/20 catalog announcements.
      exact_resume_boundary: Extend only `tinyrustlm/tools/vnext-campaign-release-surface.js` with strict forward-only deployment receipts and production HTTPS exact-byte/hash readback descendants over the authorized r5/v3 manifest. Then add generated pointer/history descendants, evidence-bound published claim.v2 descendants, and current site-publisher signatures. Reject fixtures, loopback/local reachability, redirects, content encoding, source or byte drift, expired authority, replay, cyclic ancestry, secrets, caller truth, and generated-document backreferences. Cut maintained entry points and delete the superseded mutable release stack after the replacement is verified, with no compatibility path.
    phase_3_deployment_attempt_admission_checkpoint:
      status: This containing source-controlled checkpoint extends only the sole r5/v3 campaign release surface with immutable deployment-attempt admission. It is not deployment success, production HTTPS readback, publication, live campaign evidence, or Phase 3 completion.
      deployment_truth_boundary: `admitDeploymentAttempt` accepts one closed data-only input over an existing prepared and authorized release. It reconstructs the exact runner operation, projection, receipt and subject snapshots, release evidence, preparation scans, stored release-authorizer signature, and its redaction receipt; then reruns the current authority graph at deployment verification time. It accepts no deployed, succeeded, published, done, readback, counter, caller verdict, mutable pointer, or fixture truth.
      exact_attempt_contract: The only admitted child is one canonical `deployment` receipt with phase/type `deployment`, status `pass`, runtime execution class `deployment`, and mandatory scope `deployment-attempt-only`. Here `pass` authenticates only the bounded attempt record, never the remote result. The current web build is its sole phase dependency; the campaign attestation uses the dedicated attestation field; and release authorization is an exact receipt reference plus public parameter, so deployment remains classifiable by the closed phase-currentness graph. The receipt also binds the release-manifest canonical hash, r5/v3 static inventory identity, deployment manifest, publication generator, security-header profile, public HTTPS origin, asset count, total bytes, submitted inventory, and one bounded transcript digest. Its attempt begins after stored authorization admission and completes no later than trusted verification time.
      redaction_persistence_and_replay: The final canonical attempt receipt is scanned against the same protected equality set used throughout preparation. On pass, its deterministic redaction receipt is create-only persisted before the deployment receipt. The only admitted store states are exact-authorized, exact-authorized-plus-redaction, and exact-authorized-plus-redaction-plus-deployment; byte-identical replay recovers either write. Unsafe deployment bytes persist only the bounded failed redaction receipt and never the deployment receipt. Any unrelated active receipt or subject blocks admission.
      frozen_facts: Release-surface profile is 9,167 bytes with SHA-256 `d867dc809b5fc1f504469edfd25c7b1f3b93e8448ba5571558f6a5f4b9079bed`; release-surface source is 120,798 bytes with SHA-256 `6c35c108350fec36c675176f9c613b8dc8150e99f7436cf9a27ba5e1a9afa0ee`; and its 77,318-byte test is SHA-256 `947cec1dc4a91b3bf3187a4dd332a0f4c8523ebd7954c38d55c232b927530dfa`.
      verification: The complete release-surface suite passed 21/21 before the phase-parent correction; the final deployment admission pair then passed 2/2 and the phase-currentness suite passed 10/10, including a direct `current-pass` assertion over the web-build/deployment graph. The contract/inventory/threat set passed 12/12. Final complete `npm run test:unit` over the corrected bytes passed 860/860 with zero failures, skips, cancellations, or todos in 378.264 seconds. JavaScript syntax, strict JSON parsing, and `git diff --check` passed.
      documentation_and_deployment_truth: The release-surface architecture, contract guidance, and contract inventory are updated in the same checkpoint. Exactly zero changed files intersect the 21 production source members in `tinyrustlm/deploy/web-deployment-manifest.v2.json`; generated release bytes are also unchanged. No version, Updates entry, site deployment, release receipt, production readback claim, or campaign counter was created.
      campaign_truth: Live progress remains 0/20 qualifying models, 0/50 deletion-backed clean-browser rounds, 0/25 authorized live memory rounds, 0/40 outside-network lane proofs, and 0/20 catalog announcements.
      exact_resume_boundary: Add strict production HTTPS exact-byte readback as the next forward-only child of one admitted deployment attempt. Resolve and pin only public addresses, retain TLS hostname verification, forbid redirects and content encoding, request identity bytes, stream with exact byte bounds, require status/type/cache/security headers, hash every static response, and bind the complete observation inventory in one create-only `public-readback` receipt. Fixtures, loopback, LAN, caller responses, partial inventories, stale authorization, byte drift, and local-only reachability must never produce a public pass. Then generate and bind the two publication descendants, create evidence-bound published claim.v2 children, verify current site-publisher signatures, cut maintained entry points, and delete the old release stack without aliases.
    phase_3_public_https_verifier_checkpoint:
      status: Code commit `900a3f304f41ff92de851072679936e6a7acb3be` is pushed and remote-exact. It adds the sole standalone production HTTPS exact-byte verifier and frozen profile. It is not yet invoked by the release surface, writes no receipt, was not run against production, establishes no outside-network independence, changes no campaign counter, and does not complete Phase 3.
      exact_boundary: `performVnextPublicHttpsReadback` accepts only one canonical DNS HTTPS root, the sorted exact r5/v3 static inventory, and canonical frozen security-header bytes. It captures Node DNS/HTTPS at module load and accepts no caller resolver, transport, response, body, retry policy, success bit, or alternate profile. It rejects any malformed or nonpublic DNS member, pins one public address after bootstrap transport success, verifies each connected remote address, uses normal TLS hostname authorization and TLS 1.2/1.3, forbids redirects, content encoding, transfer encoding, ranges, cookies, and transformed bodies, and streams every asset once to exact length and SHA-256.
      web_and_header_contract: The verifier rejects project-hosted model routes, extra or invalid bootstraps, invalid service-worker policy, stable immutable paths, unsafe path encodings, unknown roles/media types/cache policies, and aggregate limit drift before DNS. Every response requires status 200, one canonical Content-Length, exact media type with only the bounded UTF-8 exception, exact cache control, the complete exact-once security-header profile, strong CSP/isolation/referrer/HSTS/nosniff/frame/permissions baselines, a complete response, and exact manifest bytes.
      result_and_privacy: The canonical result binds profile/source/security identities, origin, counts, sorted per-asset observations, and domain-separated complete-DNS-set, pinned-address, certificate-set, and observation-inventory identities. It returns no raw body, raw headers, address, certificate, credential, host path, or receipt authority. Pure exported fixture helpers cannot create the production result through caller-injected transport and never count as live readback.
      frozen_facts: Profile `contracts/vnext/public-https-readback-profile.v1.json` has SHA-256 `0cfeb00065d45fd860813f501d6c07417f8a6e6587dd524a81e5be426a84c419`; source SHA-256 is `b7d03950690761e63271dfca4734d16f75d5dd698f3c2326b29f2bf7f3dbf948`; test SHA-256 is `ee469ae358d0d93d3553dc69aeb99913f5ad6ad14388279d5c4326a11acf5fdc`; and the dedicated architecture account SHA-256 is `d1f9097a7ec159e16f9fa03c7b2f8f1cad2a7bf7c6cd5ad2d89bf62c4568581a`.
      verification: Focused verifier tests passed 9/9. The final fast affected contract/inventory/threat/redaction/verifier set passed 31/31 with zero failures, skips, cancellations, or todos. JavaScript syntax, frozen-profile self-validation, `git diff --check`, and a high-confidence sensitive-token scan passed. A redundant combined run containing the long synthetic release-surface suite was intentionally terminated after several quiet minutes to prioritize the user's requested source-control and site-release audit; no failure was emitted, but that terminated run is not counted as pass. The prior unchanged release surface remains proven at its pushed deployment-attempt checkpoint.
      documentation_and_deployment_truth: The dedicated architecture page, contract guidance, adjacent release-surface account, and threat addendum changed with the verifier. No production deployment-manifest member changed, and the verifier is not yet integrated into the immutable release receipt graph, so no version, Updates entry, deployment, production readback claim, or campaign counter was created. A seven-site audit reconfirmed that TinyRustLM.com 0.2.1 remains the only immutable successful-publication receipt; every other site retains its recorded ledger/test/tooling blocker.
      exact_resume_boundary: Extend only `tinyrustlm/tools/vnext-campaign-release-surface.js`. Reconstruct one admitted deployment attempt and current release authorization, invoke the production verifier inside that operation, scan canonical result and receipt bytes, and create-only persist redaction before one exact `public-readback` receipt with dependency-prefix crash recovery and byte-identical replay. Then add generated pointer/history, evidence-bound published claim.v2, and current site-publisher descendants; cut maintained entry points; and delete the superseded release stack without aliases or dual readers.
    phase_3_public_readback_admission_checkpoint:
      status: Code commit `316b74fac98863e2e37d9b78b3380902393c1dc3` is pushed and remote-exact. The sole release surface now invokes the frozen production HTTPS verifier only after exact stored deployment-attempt and current release-authorization reconstruction, independently validates the canonical result, scans finalized bytes, and create-only persists one forward-only `public-readback` receipt. The committed automated proof uses an explicitly fixture-labeled process substitution and is not a production run, public reachability receipt, outside-network proof, publication, or campaign evidence.
      exact_operation: `verifyPublicReadback` accepts one closed data-only input and rejects caller transport, response, resolver, verdict, pass, deployed, published, done, fixture, or counter truth. It reconstructs the prepared lineage and exact stored deployment receipt plus its deterministic redaction receipt, reruns current release-authorizer authority, invokes `performVnextPublicHttpsReadback` internally, and independently verifies every result descriptor, origin, count, asset observation, cache/security policy, response hash and length, DNS/certificate/address identity, verifier profile, and verifier source identity against the immutable r5/v3 manifest.
      persistence_and_recovery: The operation scans the canonical verifier result against the protected equality set, builds and scans the final receipt, and create-only persists the readback redaction before the readback receipt. Exact store prefixes admit the authorized deployment state, redaction-only interruption state, and complete readback state. Retry reruns the deterministic verifier, completes only byte-identical descendants, and returns an existing-byte-identical replay without overwriting history. Unrelated descendants, malformed results, unsafe bytes, stale authority, source drift, or dependency drift fail closed.
      frozen_facts: Release-surface profile is 11,271 bytes with SHA-256 `504492d9314b0751f09b2110b92cd7b2d5b284a11506b00b82d46ec9f0c4d7db`; release-surface source is 149,977 bytes with SHA-256 `d18bad2b0bdf478dbd2a0b7bde7f0f2af10bf041205d2bf366ff5f9c201b4a0d`; and its 90,784-byte test is SHA-256 `676e63b349ecd34dc706737b28d377676742d29b888fea7b5af1dd6afe402747`. The standalone verifier profile remains `0cfeb00065d45fd860813f501d6c07417f8a6e6587dd524a81e5be426a84c419`.
      verification: The final complete release-surface suite passed 22/22 with zero failures, skips, cancellations, or todos in 407.239 seconds. The adjacent receipt-store, redaction, and phase-currentness set passed 45/45; the contract, conformance, inventory, threat, verifier, and architecture set passed 41/41; and the final threat-review subset passed 3/3. JavaScript syntax, `git diff --check`, stale active-profile search, explicit debt-marker review, changed-file high-confidence secret scan, and exact production-manifest intersection passed. Zero of 21 production source members changed.
      documentation_and_deployment_truth: Contract guidance, release-surface architecture, verifier integration guidance, contract inventory, and threat review were updated in the same code commit. Because no production closure member changed and no authorized production operation was run, no version, Updates entry, deployment, release receipt, public readback claim, or campaign counter was created. All seven production URLs returned HTTP 200 after their intended redirects during the bounded availability audit; availability is not publication evidence.
      campaign_truth: Live progress remains 0/20 qualifying models, 0/50 deletion-backed clean-browser rounds, 0/25 authorized live memory rounds, 0/40 outside-network lane proofs, and 0/20 catalog announcements.
      exact_resume_boundary: Add the two generated publication-file descendants and exact immutable history, then create evidence-bound published `claim.v2` descendants and verify current site-publisher signatures. Maintain an acyclic forward-only graph, prohibit generated-document backreferences and caller publication truth, and preserve strict create-only replay and redaction at each publication boundary. After replacement verification, cut maintained entry points and delete the superseded release stack without aliases, dual readers, or compatibility behavior. Complete the Rust/Win32 directory-flush helper, compressed archive-member scanning, and protected equality-list custody before production durability or publication claims.
    completed_phase_gate: ADR-001 through ADR-011 are accepted in `docs/architecture/adr/`; they freeze metadata grammar, SHA-256/Merkle identity, alignment/layout, companion transport, browser persistence, quantization profiles, WebGPU support, specialist composition, service-worker release behavior, evidence signing, and the sole campaign-evidence browser boundary.
    completed_contract_increment: `tinyrustlm/tools/strict-json.js` now provides bounded fatal-UTF-8 duplicate-aware parsing, and all three release-authorization files pass through it before schema or Ed25519 verification. The verifier tool hash binds both modules and identifies profile `tinyrustlm.strict-json.v1`; hostile tests cover literal/escaped/supplementary duplicate names, invalid UTF-8, BOMs, lone surrogates, depth/entry/string limits, unsafe numbers, negative zero, overflow/underflow, malformed grammar, and trailing data.
    prior_completed_contract_inventory: The pushed checkpoint recorded 215 dated schema IDs across 109 app/tool files, canonical-list SHA-256 `581eee525ee30f195f0a21cd71db8d60ff275866d51cb2d236df74f638bd6d10`, and 166 `JSON.parse` calls across 77 files. Those numbers are historical checkpoint facts; the current work-in-progress inventory above supersedes them for the dirty worktree.
    prior_completed_contract_freeze: The pushed checkpoint registry was 37,361 bytes with SHA-256 `432188d01b5ad7c7cd535d7df4924627ec288eb8be15c251e09dd949ed767818`. That hash and the later r4 checkpoint remain immutable historical evidence but are not active contracts; current r5 registry facts are recorded in `phase_3_exact_web_publication_graph_checkpoint`.
    prior_completed_validator_checkpoint: The earlier pushed checkpoint corpus had 69 cases and 138 matching validator verdicts. Those results remain historical checkpoint evidence; current corpus and validator facts are recorded in `phase_3_acyclic_release_contract_checkpoint` and passed the named focused and complete sets.
    prior_completed_phase_2_threat_review: The pushed threat review recorded PASS only for its bound schema-and-local-invariant boundary. The current work updates that review and its bound inputs for the proof-v2 correction; no production cutover, cryptographic authority graph, model quality, browser round, live memory, public P2P, catalog, package, site, or campaign authority is granted.
    remaining_contract_risk: Exact campaign-plan finalization, semantic currentness, Ed25519 verification, authority graph, offline-bundle closure, truthful projection, projection-result validation, generated browser transport, exact cross-store snapshots, immutable operations, process exclusion, old-runner deletion, fresh-runner-bound final attestation, canonical public-document and release-text scanning, protected equality scanning, derived operator status, exact create-only unauthorized release-manifest preparation, current release-authorizer admission, bounded immutable deployment-attempt admission, caller-noninjected production HTTPS verification, and immutable public-readback admission now have independent Rust-backed or bounded host evidence where applicable. Phase 3 remains incomplete. Generated publication descendants, published claim.v2 creation, site-publisher authorization, clean deletion of the superseded release stack, production-grade Windows directory durability, compressed archive-member scanning, and protected-list release custody remain incomplete. Existing dated evidence and fixture-labeled readback proof are historical or local only and cannot satisfy production gates.
    exact_next_action: Extend only `tinyrustlm/tools/vnext-campaign-release-surface.js` with the two generated publication-file descendants, immutable history, evidence-bound published `claim.v2` descendants, and current site-publisher signatures. Reject fixtures, loopback or local reachability as public proof, expired authorization, replay, source drift, byte mismatch, cyclic ancestry, generated-document backreferences, secrets, and caller publication truth. Cut maintained entry points and documentation to this completed surface and delete the old dashboard, final-attestation, release-authorization, release-evidence, public-readback, public-artifact-scope, and obsolete store paths without aliases or dual readers. In parallel, complete the Rust/Win32 directory-flush helper, compressed archive-member scanning, and protected equality-list custody. Commit and push every coherent major change immediately after its affected build/checks pass; deploy each affected site whenever its complete release gate passes, and never fabricate a release when production closure bytes are unchanged.
    no_compatibility_shims: SLM2 and the vNext schema family are intentionally incompatible clean contracts. Do not retain SLM1 fallback, old aliases, dual readers/writers, conversion-kit downloads, or user-run handoff scripts in the new product path.
  verified_test_baseline:
    architecture_decision_tests: `node --test tests/architecture-decisions.test.js` passed 13, failed 0, skipped 0 with ADR-001 through ADR-011 present and accepted.
    strict_json_release_boundary_tests: `node --test tests/strict-json.test.js tests/campaign-release-authorization-evidence.test.js` passed 12, failed 0, skipped 0.
    vnext_contract_inventory_tests: `node --test tests/vnext-contract-inventory.test.js` passed 3, failed 0, skipped 0.
    vnext_contract_registry_tests: `node --test tests/vnext-contract-registry.test.js` passed 6, failed 0, skipped 0; the tests strictly parse the registry, reconcile it to the nine-name inventory, validate every descriptor/reference/cardinality/identity exclusion, enforce explicit signing/context/redaction/claim fields, freeze finite parser/redaction rules, and reject compatibility acceptance surfaces.
    vnext_validator_and_threat_review_tests: `node --test tests/vnext-contract-registry.test.js tests/vnext-contract-validator-conformance.test.js tests/vnext-contract-threat-review.test.js` passed 16, failed 0, skipped 0. Both validators matched all 82 expected corpus verdicts; source-independence, corpus regeneration, invariant partitioning, property checks, bound threat-review hashes, deferred obligations, and no-shim validator surfaces are enforced.
