  campaign_progress:
    qualified_distinct_model_hashes: `0/20`
    deletion_backed_clean_browser_rounds: `0/50`
    authorized_live_memory_continuity_rounds: `0/25`
    current_outside_network_lane_proofs: `0/40`
    live_catalog_announcements: `0/20`
    evidence_basis: The active worktree has no campaign directory or objective receipt set satisfying these gates. Historical experiments, model fixtures, local/LAN/loopback tests, mocked services, package creation, source conversion, structural validation, and isolated browser smokes do not increment any counter.
    completion_rule: Never report `done`, `passed`, public P2P availability, model qualification, MemoryEndpoints continuity, or publication from unit tests alone. Partial evidence stays visible and blockers cannot become skips or simulated passes.
  active_external_blockers:
    - Twenty genuinely useful, distinct, provenance-bound models and the training/qualification compute and human review needed to earn 20/20 do not yet exist as current objective receipts.
    - This session is not connected to MemoryEndpoints.com; the authoritative production single-use enrollment/reconnect/cleanup contract and authorized disposable-company credentials are unavailable, so live continuity remains 0/25.
    - No authorized independent outside-network observer and current signed complete-transfer receipts exist for 40 public lanes, so outside proof remains 0/40 and catalog announcement remains 0/20.
    - Required real-hardware execution evidence, including physical `linux-arm64`, remains distinct from cross-compilation, binary inspection, or emulation and is not complete.
    - Role-separated campaign evidence keys, trust registry, publication authorization, and all non-TinyRustLM site release ledgers must be provisioned and verified before their corresponding claims can close.
    - MiniModel.org `master` has a pre-existing release-gate defect: its full Rust workspace run reaches tests but fails 21 `minimodel-core` cases because checked-in peer-offer proof hashes differ from admission hashes; its Node catalog set passes 11/12 and fails the published announcement-feed hash binding. The documentation-policy commit is isolated from those inputs, but MiniModel publication remains blocked until the defects are repaired and the full gate passes.
    - Runtime.MiRust.com's PowerShell verifier throws an `Invoke-WebRequest` null-reference on its first HEAD request under the installed Windows PowerShell. Independent `curl` observed the intended `301` to the developer portal and subsequent `200`, but that does not repair the verifier. PHP is unavailable locally, so PHP syntax validation was not executed. Runtime publication remains blocked on a working verifier and complete release gate.
    - The current `PLUTO\AI` process cannot write the six existing `E:\Source\Rust\{site}\.uai\totem.uai` files because those checkouts grant write access to other Windows identities only. Remote policy commits are authoritative and exact; protected local checkouts remain stale until their owner updates permissions or refreshes them. Do not delete or replace those files to bypass the ACL.
  related_site_account:
    inventory_scope: Direct site roots under `E:\Source\Rust`; current routing lives in the mutable `E:\Source\Rust\workspace.uai`, while the bounded public observations below are dated 2026-08-09. A live response, source commit, package version, HTTP Last-Modified value, and immutable publication receipt are different evidence classes and are labeled separately below.
    LMComposer.com: Retired alias. The local root now contains `.uai/totem.uai` with policy `site-family-documentation-integrity-v1`, but it has no Git repository or remote. Production responds with a redirect to TinyRustLM.com. Last publication is unknown because no immutable site release ledger exists; source-control enrollment remains blocked.
    MiniModel.MiRust.com: Active documentation-first MiniModel developer and protocol reference. Remote `master` is policy commit `f462195e7af2b08f08edcd190d848560495cd287`; the protected local checkout remains at `3c5f9e28c48fd2b843f58df91accc5579a3270a5` until its owner refreshes it. The prior observed live root was byte-identical to that older local commit and returned Last-Modified `2026-07-12T22:33:49Z`; this is not publication authority and the new policy commit is not claimed deployed.
    MiniModel.org: Active catalog and direct-P2P discovery surface with required user, developer, and operator documentation; it must never proxy model bytes. Remote `master` is policy commit `6718981631e6e6a5efcd9b5d44216d1cfc6c4083`; the protected local checkout remains at `693c50f0fa2a82fd502dfc9d38c0e140531850da`. Full Rust and Node gates expose the recorded pre-existing hash-drift failures, so publication is blocked and the policy commit is not claimed deployed.
    MiRust.com: Active documentation, evidence, marketing, architecture, research, and governance authority. Remote `master` is policy commit `b3dcbb90337d3e19a3da09c9b575aa5cc963c09b`; the protected local checkout remains at `6dd665033c1d3a8ef907ee3140707a6fcb4c0357`. The live footer still reports latest content update `2026-06-25T16:42:00Z` and Theme/Core `2.3.0`; no new deployment is claimed and no immutable release ledger exists.
    Runtime.MiRust.com: Retired redirect with bounded historical evidence, currently routing to `https://tinyrustlm.mirust.com/developer-portal/`. Remote `master` is policy commit `8cb141dc9c0387c5fcf37e6f7dbc9af83352fa6e`; the protected local checkout remains at `3bf5a5de50d21c4a10e8dd08dffa1eabd83199fc`. Independent HTTPS observation found the expected `301` then `200`, but the declared verifier is defective and no deployment or immutable publication is claimed.
    TinyRustLM.com: Active browser-local product surface. Code commit `af99ffa4a6e45babcffb184e974fda6b20d71f1d` is pushed and remote-exact on `codex/model-acquisition-v2`; it adds canonical public release-text scanning and transitive Node/Rust parity while changing zero production deployment-manifest members. The current immutable ledger still records only `tinyrustlm.com@0.2.1`, release date `2026-08-08`, published `2026-08-08T23:47:22.420Z`, source revision `e964a095ede1c077b36b6476af5ee85b087f52f8`, and publication ID `aea1e08b74f6b7835473ffb482baeddd42c97346d0a08868a66574f1a5d089ce`. Internal evidence changes have no deployable web-byte delta and create no new site release.
    TinyRustLM.MiRust.com: Active documentation-first TinyRustLM architecture, developer, and evidence portal. Remote `master` is policy commit `5ebbf32f31b54a3cc9637008d7020b46f832064c`; the protected local checkout remains at `c9cd240221c6ff6efd7ab5fcc476dad96f75ad01`. Local/live identity remains observed as `1.6.0`, updated `2026-07-12T22:00:00Z`; PHP is unavailable locally and no new deployment or immutable publication is claimed.
  publication_discipline:
    - Commit and push every coherent major change as soon as its affected build and checks are healthy. Do not hold a valid checkpoint for unrelated future perfection.
    - Publish every affected site promptly when its complete affected release gate passes. Internal-only changes with no deployable site-byte delta do not create a release. A failing build, test, documentation, security, authorization, transport, or readback gate remains an explicit blocker and never becomes a skip.
    - Before each site publish, assign an intentional semantic version and release date, update a human-readable update log plus an immutable machine-readable release ledger, bind the exact clean source revision and artifact hashes, run relevant tests and secret scans, and obtain publication authorization.
    - Commit and push every affected source, documentation, marketing, and release-log repository before claiming publication. Deploy only from its source-control truth, then verify public HTTPS readback, version, release date, update log, asset hashes, and behavior.
    - Keep TinyRustLM.com, TinyRustLM.MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, MiniModel.MiRust.com, MiRust.com, and any retained redirect surfaces behaviorally and editorially consistent. Record an explicit blocker when a site cannot be updated; never call local files, package creation, upload attempts, or stale pages deployed.
    - Bring every retained active site onto one consistent immutable release-ledger contract; TinyRustLM.com is currently the only site in this inventory with `uaix.site_release.v1` publication evidence.
version_authority:
  current_version: 0.2.1
  next_version: 0.2.2
  policy: Increment intentionally after real implementation milestones; source scaffolding does not imply runtime support.
active_product:
  name: TinyRustLM
  root: tinyrustlm/
  purpose: Zero-dependency Rust/WASM browser-local SLM runtime and UI.
  enterprise_vnext_development_goal_2026_08_01: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-enterprise-vnext-development-goal-memory-2026-08-01.md`, SHA256 `22838f84d8df1b7daef4577fa5f52fdbcf31e7f20eeeb377bf2b6f092c5b5731`, routes the 25-report enterprise vNext synthesis and active 60,899-byte execution assignment, SHA256 `629d7bee195f80c4acb868ed90c4124fd80d2cf6a1060a8fe13fdaa65968b31a`. It requires clean incompatible contracts, ten ADR gates, scalar-first conformance, bounded browser/runtime/security/release work, champion-plus-sealed-specialists, immutable evidence, and synchronized sites. The reports are advisory and every 20/50/25/40/20 campaign counter remains unearned until objective receipts exist.
  pre_release_no_debt_authority_2026_07_15: TinyRustLM is not a live released product. Until the human explicitly removes this rule, add no technical debt, legacy support, backward-compatibility paths, dual contracts, migration shims, deprecated aliases, or knowingly temporary architecture. Clean replacement, deletion of superseded implementation after verification, and full rewrites are authorized. Immutable receipts and dated failure evidence remain historical truth, not supported product behavior. This authority supersedes incompatible present-tense wording in older dated workspace entries.
  model_acquisition_v2_authority_2026_08_08: The current acquisition contract supersedes older conversion-kit and import-kit workflow entries. One user action selects a model. A complete identity-matched MiniModel P2P offer with its composition graph is preferred and is imported through the paired local companion; otherwise, after explicit companion pairing, protocol v2 performs immutable reviewed Hugging Face source download, bounded resumable hashing, Rust conversion, Rust receipt reinspection, `.slm` validation, base-only `.acg1` creation, composition reinspection, direct loopback streaming, and browser activation. Progress and typed failures stay in the app. Model acquisition and P2P sharing must not download README/TXT, shell, PowerShell, request JSON, conversion-kit, share-kit, or serving-helper files and must not require users to run scripts. TinyRustLM.com, MiniModel.org, UAIX.org, and MemoryEndpoints.com receive no prompts, responses, source tensors, model bytes, or composition bytes. Browser-only local `.slm` import remains valid; companion access is explicit, scoped, session-bound, and never probed before consent. The packaged companion and Rust converter are version 0.2.0 for this contract; release and public-deployment claims remain pending objective gates.
  third_party_review_storage_authority_2026_07_21: Keep all downloaded third-party repositories, packages, papers, standards, source archives, and model-review inputs outside project repositories and Git under `E:\Source\external\{project-name}`. Source control may contain original TinyRustLM work plus public-safe URLs, immutable revisions, byte counts, hashes, licenses, and bounded findings, but not copied third-party review trees or machine-local external paths.
  source_control_model_payload_boundary_2026_07_26: Current source control contains no candidate, trained, converted, product, source-checkpoint, raw-tensor, or P2P-piece model payloads. Only six explicitly allowlisted deterministic `.slm` fixtures of at most 64 KiB remain, and they are runtime/test evidence only. Browser boot has no built-in model and requires admitted local, selector-registry, companion, or P2P intake. A preservation-only external manifest with SHA256 `96795962727efcae9ee142ba31a4de7b8d891e176ef6373a6a518383e2155bca` reverified 6 `.slm` artifacts plus 8 source checkpoints, 16,259,130,576 total bytes, and zero partial files; it grants no quality, release, catalog, or campaign-counter authority. Older entries naming tracked model paths or bootstrap selectors are immutable history, not current product behavior.
  exact_flat_named_target_performance_2026_07_22: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-named-target-performance-memory-2026-07-22.md`, SHA256 `20620ef887db16098a3d7de942c101653fba77aee06cb1951f9c3a4e23e71a68`, routes preregistration SHA256 `269459766b1bab57ce86cadda296d0941d3dfc3d6876873ab48657ba7bd64c63`, preserved pre-execution failure `exact-flat-physical-target-attempt-1291be20cc291bc6`, observation `exact-flat-physical-target-20bfb3e18230f257`, and child receipt `exact-flat-physical-target-verification-6b478318ef8747cb` file SHA256 `4cf29cef23b057677e97ed0e03751bac6ad88d31fe44dff2d93582c22d437c1e`. Three preregistered workloads and 324 retained query samples verify latency, throughput, and process memory only on the named Windows host. Energy, independent chassis attestation, complete physical-target status, sealed-corpus quality, crash-recovered deletion, compression, product, training, and release remain false. Never rerun either physical-target `--write` command.
  exact_flat_browser_wasm_verification_2026_07_21: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-browser-wasm-verification-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `b9191b867784c8c0323c8f2b484aca5c13c95a5766686a3da061cb35d83150a7`, routes v2 preregistration, committed runner, immutable observation `exact-flat-browser-wasm-0361d72f245abbd3` file SHA256 `d28c921ec1df7db538417aaed8803fce88bc6d37b3cbc5fcf5d291b0a91a6f9a`, and child receipt `exact-flat-browser-wasm-verification-8fcdeb0b93534ca4` file SHA256 `5c52a2287390f79e6a4971da6a6455a69c4ebd52ac6473bcce5408fd62560157`. The exact three-module, 49-test set ran in two real Chromium processes; all entry points returned zero, processes closed, unique profiles were deleted, and page-network/error counters were zero. This grants only exact experiment real-browser execution; use the newer named-target route for bounded host measurements. Sealed-corpus quality, durable deletion, compression, TurboVec parity, product, training, and release remain unproved. Never rerun either browser `--write` command.
